//! The client's instance table: `GAME_SMSG_0x01A0`, transcribed from a live load.
//!
//! Generated by hand once from `recordings/client/feature/maps/pre-searing-load-3.jsonl`, the load of
//! instance 148, which carries ten such messages. Each entry is `(instance, value)`: the instance id is the
//! number every other message in this tree uses (148 for Ascalon City), and the second number is the one a
//! live server sent with it - four instances at a time share a value, so it is a per-base-map or per-region
//! identity rather than an instance of its own. Nothing in this tree computes it, and nothing may: it is
//! game data, so it is copied.
//!
//! **Ten values are missing, and this file does not invent them.** Every recorded message is four bytes
//! short of its own struct: the last pair's instance id arrives and its value does not (the first record
//! ends `0c 03 00 00`, instance 780, with no value behind it). So the pairs below are exactly those the
//! capture holds - 137 of 147 - and the ten that lost their value are absent rather than zero-filled.
//! A re-capture, or a read of the same context through the instrument, is what would fill them.

